["er.eventlog.import-anchor/1",{"authority":{"logical_scope":"aep","stream_identity":"01a0cae6-7e88-710c-8913-d70d29cb7b4c","tenant":"planning"},"completeness":"available_evidence_only","evidence":[],"instance":{"entity":"aep.entity","fields":{"document":{"events":[],"fields":{"$aep":{"archived":false,"metadata":{"created_at":0,"id":"MIG941b8737042e8251996e577c5811f65e85f90abafde8e8e1be239c9cece34dc6","locator":"ep://planning/store/story/machine-readable-service-contract","provenance":{"created_by":"system","updated_by":"system"},"revision":7,"type":"aep.story/v1","updated_at":0}},"body":"## Context\n\nThe independently implemented service needs to publish OpenAPI from the EP-owned wire. Deriving schemas or routes again in the service would create a second source of truth beside the DTOs and client paths already verified by the conformance corpus.\n\n## Acceptance\n\nEvery public request/response wire DTO implements JSON Schema from its actual Serde shape; one typed catalog names every method, path template and accepted media type; the official client consumes the catalog rather than private path literals; generated schemas accept every constructed conformance document; and no existing v1/v2 encoded byte changes.\n","relations":[{"serves":"vision:O2"},{"serves":"vision:O6"},{"informed_by":"story:aep-service-wire-and-client"}],"scope":[{"confidence":"inferred","path":"crates/edge/aep-cli/src/serve"},{"confidence":"cited","path":"crates/plan/aep-client"},{"confidence":"inferred","path":"crates/plan/aep-conformance"}],"status":"draft","summary":"Give consumers schema-enabled wire DTOs and one typed route/media catalog without changing v1 or v2 bytes.","title":"Publish the service wire as machine-readable schema and routes"},"lifecycle_state":"draft"}},"id":"MIG941b8737042e8251996e577c5811f65e85f90abafde8e8e1be239c9cece34dc6","lifecycle_state":"recorded","revision":7,"version":1},"order":"per_kind_only","subject":["aep.entity","MIG941b8737042e8251996e577c5811f65e85f90ab